From ac85fe79975c9d14aeedbb62a3d97f5dbf1c139c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:35:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] fix(engine): test membership in a set of records as TLC's
 toRcd reads the value

SetOfRcdsValue.member takes the record `toRcd` makes of the value and
fails on a value it makes none of. `toRcd` makes the empty record of
the empty tuple, and of a function only where every key is a string.
The compiled set of records failed on the empty tuple, where TLC finds
it isn't a member, and took a function with other keys for a record
that isn't a member, where TLC fails; the lazy set and the trace
evaluator already read it as TLC does. 7 runs of the upstream
conformance suite that declined now match, and one that printed
FALSE where TLC fails now declines.
